From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AX23_V2_OPENWRT <ax23-v2-openwrt@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:47:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: archer-ax23-v2: make every partition
 read-only

This port has no validated installation or recovery procedure yet, so a
RAM-booted image must not be able to write NAND at all. Four partitions
were still writable:

- "data" holds the stock firmware's empty UBI (4 PEBs, no user volume).
  The generic UBI auto-attach (pending 490) attaches a partition named
  "data" on every boot, so the RAM image attached it read-write and
  started its background thread; boot logs from an AX21 v5 running this
  image show "UBI: auto-attach mtd15" and "ubi0: attached mtd15 (name
  "data")" without the write-protected notice that tp_data gets. UBI
  may erase or scrub PEBs on its own once attached read-write.
- 0:APPSBLENV only needs to be read (fw_printenv, uboot-envtools).
- rootfs / rootfs_1 are the stock dual-boot slots; sysupgrade is already
  refused on this board.

With all sixteen partitions read-only, UBI attaches "data" in read-only
mode like tp_data, and nothing in the kernel can write to the flash.
Dropping read-only from the slots and the environment belongs with a
reviewed, hardware-validated installation procedure.
---
 .../qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts      | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
index b8d916fffe..3b7c0f0158 100644
--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/dts/ipq5018-archer-ax23-v2.dts
@@ -385,6 +385,16 @@
 		nand-ecc-step-size = <512>;
 		nand-bus-width = <8>;
 
+		/*
+		 * Every partition is read-only while this port has no validated
+		 * installation and recovery procedure: a RAM-booted image must not
+		 * be able to write NAND at all. In particular the stock "data"
+		 * partition holds an empty UBI that the generic auto-attach (490)
+		 * would otherwise attach read-write with a background thread, and
+		 * 0:APPSBLENV only needs to be read (fw_printenv). Drop read-only
+		 * from the slots and APPSBLENV only together with a reviewed,
+		 * hardware-validated installation procedure.
+		 */
 		partitions {
 			compatible = "fixed-partitions";
 			#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -435,6 +445,7 @@
 			partition@300000 {
 				label = "0:APPSBLENV";
 				reg = <0x300000 0x080000>;
+				read-only;
 			};
 
 			partition@380000 {
@@ -458,11 +469,13 @@
 			partition@640000 {
 				label = "rootfs";
 				reg = <0x640000 0x3580000>;
+				read-only;
 			};
 
 			partition@3bc0000 {
 				label = "rootfs_1";
 				reg = <0x3bc0000 0x3580000>;
+				read-only;
 			};
 
 			partition@7140000 {
@@ -480,6 +493,7 @@
 			partition@7dc0000 {
 				label = "data";
 				reg = <0x7dc0000 0x080000>;
+				read-only;
 			};
 		};
 	};
